        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is <b>to resist tensile forces</b> because concrete is weak in tension but strong in compression. Reinforcement (e.g., steel bars) compensates for this weakness by absorbing tensile stresses. It does not primarily resist compression, shear, or improve workability.</p>",
